$PQ=QR$, so the triangle is isosceles.

$\begin{aligned}PQ^2+QR^2&=10+10\\&=20\\&=PR^2\end{aligned}$

The side lengths satisfy Pythagoras' theorem. The right angle is at $Q$, opposite $PR$.

