examples.question_text:
Quadrilateral $ABCD$ has vertices $A(0,0)$, $B(4,1)$, $C(6,4)$ and $D(2,3)$. Show that it is a parallelogram using:

a. the midpoints of its diagonals;

b. the gradients of its opposite sides.

examples.solution_text:
a.

$\begin{aligned}M_{AC}&=\left(\frac{0+6}{2},\frac{0+4}{2}\right)=(3,2)\\M_{BD}&=\left(\frac{4+2}{2},\frac{1+3}{2}\right)=(3,2)\end{aligned}$

The diagonals have the same midpoint, so they bisect each other. Therefore $ABCD$ is a parallelogram.

b.

$\begin{aligned}m_{AB}&=\frac{1-0}{4-0}=\frac14\\m_{DC}&=\frac{4-3}{6-2}=\frac14\\m_{BC}&=\frac{4-1}{6-4}=\frac32\\m_{AD}&=\frac{3-0}{2-0}=\frac32\end{aligned}$

$AB\parallel DC$ and $BC\parallel AD$, so $ABCD$ is a parallelogram.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=8mm,y=8mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\draw[black,thick] (0,0)--(4,1)--(6,4)--(2,3)--cycle;
\draw[black,dashed] (0,0)--(6,4) (4,1)--(2,3);
\fill[black] (3,2) circle (1.5pt);
\path (0,0) node[below left] {$A$};
\path (4,1) node[below right] {$B$};
\path (6,4) node[above right] {$C$};
\path (2,3) node[above left] {$D$};
\path (3,2) node[above right] {$M(3,2)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

a.

$\begin{aligned}AB&=\sqrt{(4-0)^2+(2-0)^2}=\sqrt{20}\\BC&=\sqrt{(6-4)^2+(6-2)^2}=\sqrt{20}\\CD&=\sqrt{(2-6)^2+(4-6)^2}=\sqrt{20}\\DA&=\sqrt{(0-2)^2+(0-4)^2}=\sqrt{20}\end{aligned}$

All four sides are equal, so $ABCD$ is a rhombus.

$\begin{aligned}AC&=\sqrt{(6-0)^2+(6-0)^2}=6\sqrt2\\BD&=\sqrt{(2-4)^2+(4-2)^2}=2\sqrt2\end{aligned}$

The diagonals are unequal, so the rhombus is not a square. Its most precise name is rhombus.

b.

$\begin{aligned}M_{AC}&=\left(\frac{0+6}{2},\frac{0+6}{2}\right)=(3,3)\\M_{BD}&=\left(\frac{4+2}{2},\frac{2+4}{2}\right)=(3,3)\\m_{AC}&=\frac{6-0}{6-0}=1\\m_{BD}&=\frac{4-2}{2-4}=-1\end{aligned}$

$m_{AC}m_{BD}=1(-1)=-1$, so the diagonals are perpendicular. Their shared midpoint shows that they bisect each other. Perpendicular bisecting diagonals establish a rhombus; their unequal lengths exclude a square.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=8mm,y=8mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\draw[black,thick] (0,0)--(4,2)--(6,6)--(2,4)--cycle;
\draw[black,dashed] (0,0)--(6,6) (4,2)--(2,4);
\draw[black] (3.2,3.2)--(3.4,3)--(3.2,2.8);
\fill[black] (3,3) circle (1.5pt);
\path (0,0) node[below left] {$A$};
\path (4,2) node[below right] {$B$};
\path (6,6) node[above right] {$C$};
\path (2,4) node[above left] {$D$};
\path (3,3) node[above left] {$M(3,3)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

a.

$\begin{aligned}m_{AB}&=\frac{2-0}{4-0}=\frac12\\m_{DC}&=\frac{4-2}{3-(-1)}=\frac12\\m_{BC}&=\frac{4-2}{3-4}=-2\\m_{AD}&=\frac{2-0}{-1-0}=-2\end{aligned}$

Both pairs of opposite sides are parallel. Also, $m_{AB}m_{BC}=\frac12(-2)=-1$, so adjacent sides are perpendicular. Therefore $ABCD$ is a rectangle.

b.

$\begin{aligned}AC&=\sqrt{(3-0)^2+(4-0)^2}=5\\BD&=\sqrt{(-1-4)^2+(2-2)^2}=5\\M_{AC}&=\left(\frac{0+3}{2},\frac{0+4}{2}\right)=\left(\frac32,2\right)\\M_{BD}&=\left(\frac{4+(-1)}{2},\frac{2+2}{2}\right)=\left(\frac32,2\right)\end{aligned}$

The diagonals are equal and bisect each other, confirming that $ABCD$ is a rectangle.

c.

$\begin{aligned}m_{AC}&=\frac{4-0}{3-0}=\frac43\\m_{BD}&=\frac{2-2}{-1-4}=0\end{aligned}$

Their product is $0$, so the diagonals are not perpendicular. The rectangle is not a square.

